 "note": "hands v3 (2026-10-13), for hands_v3_post.py / hands_v3_field.py, appended after P-pawrefine1 (the fore paws refined to a median edge of about .00065), in place of hands v2. Anatomy review 2026-10-13, finding 8 (Nick, 2026-10-13: \"Yes, fix all ten of them.\"); coordinator review of v2 (2026-10-13): claw 1 still showed its flat top from the side, the front toe's nail-bed hood read as a lump with a lip, the toes read as rectangular sausages with lumpy edges from below, the palm pad as a slab; cause: the paw's vertex spacing. The +x paw is described; the step runs one grid per paw (step .001) and mirrors every mass to -x. toes: rounder beans than v2 (rb .0145 at the tip, ra .011 at the knuckle, ySquash 1.3, knuckle z -.172), splayed -9, -3, 3, 9 degrees, joined toe to toe (toeToeK .005) and to the paw (toeK .005). pads: a domed palm pad (an ellipsoid .016 deep standing .004 proud), four toe pads (.0016 proud) and a nail-bed hood on the back of each toe tip (.001 proud, footprint .005 by .0055, under the toe tip's size), all joined by smooth minimums. claws: per fore claw a rotation about its base so it points along its toe, curled 15 degrees toward the palm, then seated .009 inside its toe tip, centered, 30 degrees toward the back of the toe (mirrored for -x). sheath collar off; the hood is the fold. levelZeroInside: vertices land on the new surface itself inside the part box (the refined paw's new vertices sat on the old flat faces). preSmooth 400 passes along normals, relax 300, untangle, finalUnfold, postSmooth (Taubin) 150: mover settings scaled to the finer mesh. Development variants v3a to v3d in untracked anatomy-fixes/work/08-hands/specs (this is v3d, from gen4.py). World units, +y back.",
